# name  = users.record.default_fields
# descr = default field set for a new host-system record

## the single authority for what a freshly created host-system record
## contains.  the settings payload is deliberately open [ users-zenka.yaml
## defines no field list ], so this is the ONE place that decides the starting
## shape -- an installer provisioning a node's 'root' account calls this same
## module, with no user-edit involved.
##
## returns a FRESHLY BUILT hashref on every call and is deliberately not
## cached in a <users.record.default_fields> variable : callers write into the
## record they are given, and a shared structure would let two of them
## collide.
##
## empty strings rather than absent keys : user-edit.form.schema_from_record
## derives its form from whichever keys the record carries, so a record with
## no fields renders nothing at all -- the keys are what make an empty record
## editable.

## contact is MULTI-VALUED by nature -- several addresses, including bare
## '@domain' wildcards -- so it is an ARRAY even when empty.  the shape IS the
## declaration : user-edit.form.schema_from_record turns an array into a
## collapsible LIST field, which draws a count when unfocused and expands into
## one editable row per entry when entered.  a scalar would render as a single
## plain value and silently lose that.
return {
    qw| contact |  => [],
    qw| location | => '',
};

